    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="4">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Northleoda">Norðleoda</ref> 4</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="4" corresp="#wit-h">Holdes 7 hehgerefan IIII þusend þrymsa.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="4" corresp="#wit-q">Holdes et summi prepositi quatuor milia þrimsa.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="4" corresp="#wit-d">Holdes 7 cyninges heahgerefan IIII þusend þri<hi rend="italic">m</hi>sa.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-h">Holdes and hehgerefan, iiii þusend þrymsa.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock" corresp="#wit-d">That of a <hi rend="italic">hold</hi> and a king's high-reeve 4,000 <hi rend="italic">thrymsas</hi>.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-h">For a Danish nobleman and a high reeve, four thousand thrymsas.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann">eines Höldr und königlichen [fehlt hlq] Oberlandvogts 4000 Tremissen [50 Pfund],</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">of a hold and a [royal — lacking in hlq] high-reeve 4,000 thrymsas [50 pounds],</ab>
        <note type="translator" source="#whitelock">see p. 209, n. 2</note>
        <note type="translator" source="#rabin-doml">reeve: The agent of either the king or the local landlord responsible for overseeing his master’s property.</note>
      </div>
    </body>
